# NOTE: git does not support trailing comments on pattern lines — a comment
# after a pattern becomes part of the pattern and silently matches nothing.
# Keep every comment on its own line.

# dependencies & build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Source media archives — NOT deliverables.
# The Google Takeout photo archive is ~49GB and the raw video working folder
# ~1.9GB. The site only needs the prepared copies under site/public.
#
# NOTE: the leading slash matters, and is not cosmetic. Unanchored, `Images/`
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — and because git on Windows
# sets core.ignorecase=true, the match is case-insensitive too. So `Images/`
# silently swallowed all 139 files of `site/public/images/`, and the site was
# published with no photographs at all while looking perfect locally. Anchoring
# each of these to the repository root is what confines them to the archives
# they were written for.
/Images/
/vedio/

# working artefacts
/review-shots/
/preview-thumbs/
/site/public/tmp-chk/

